{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he placed in the breastplate the Urim and the Tummim.</b> It was a parchment on which the explicit Name was written, and this was already explained in the section of ואתה תצוה. It was one of the degrees of the holy spirit (ruach ha-kodesh), below the degree of prophecy and above that of the bat kol. And know that the difference between prophecy and the holy spirit is that the prophet, at the time prophecy comes upon him, all his faculties and powers are nullified, and he is stripped of all the ways of this world and abstracted from matter and secluded with the intellect alone — and behold, this is while awake; and this is the distinction of the eight prophets. But the holy spirit is such that none of his faculties are nullified and he speaks in the manner of any man, except that a supernal spirit stirs him and the words appear upon his tongue and he speaks of future things with divine assistance; and this is the distinction of the Writings (Ketuvim). But the distinction of the Torah that Moses commanded us is above all this, for the prophecy of Moses is above all the other prophets altogether. And for this reason you find that the Sages, of blessed memory, everywhere mention Torah, Prophets, and Writings, in the order of the ranks and degrees of prophecy. And explicitly they said: one may set aside Torah for the Prophets, but not the Writings for the Prophets. All this the Sages, of blessed memory, needed to point out concerning the degrees of prophecy, so that a person may reflect, and the living may take to heart — from where does prophecy issue, and how the ranks are one above the other, and what is the difference between the prophecy of Moses and that of all the other prophets."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:01.685435468Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}